    Stop re-rendering a 1700-node tree every frame
    
    The parallax lerp called setMouseOffset on every rAF tick, re-rendering
    the whole loading screen 60x/sec. Write --mx/--my straight to the DOM
    instead and have the layers read them via calc(), so React renders once.
    The loop now also parks itself when the cursor settles rather than
    spinning forever, and skips entirely under prefers-reduced-motion.
    
    Drop sub-pixel blur from the animated particles: a per-frame filter pass
    for something invisible at 0.3px.
    
    Note: headless Chromium has a ~50ms frame floor regardless of content
    (hiding all grass changed nothing), so this is structural, not measured.
    
